{"archetypes":[{"name":"shell-set-e-invariants","focus_area":"correctness","weight":2,"rationale":"The driver pervasively toggles set +e/set -e around child calls; a missed re-enable or an early-exit path that bypasses _write_result_and_emit could silently drop the result env and trigger the mandatory-keys abort in the orchestrator.","prompt_body":"Review every `set +e` / `set -e` block in `skills/design/scripts/design-plan-quality-assessor.sh`. For each child invocation (`$SNAPSHOT_SH`, `$ASSESS_SH`, `append-tool-failure.sh`, `write-cursor` rollback), verify the exit code is captured before `set -e` is restored and that `_write_result_and_emit` is always reached on the settled exit-0 path. Check whether any failure mode (e.g., `append-tool-failure.sh` inside a `set +e` block that itself uses `rm -f`) can leave the script in a `set +e` state on the non-failure path. Also verify the SKILL.md Step 3.6 fence's outer `set +e` capture correctly restores `set -e` before the abort block. Cite specific file paths and line ranges for any issues found, and follow the output-format rules from your outer wrapper exactly.","prompt_body_end":""},{"name":"kv-parse-boundary","focus_area":"edge-cases","weight":2,"rationale":"Values in KEY=VALUE lines can contain `=` (e.g. file paths for ASSESSOR_VERDICT_FILE/ENV), and the _assessor_force_stdout / _assessor_parse_ok two-step logic in both the SKILL.md fence and apply_step3_6_handoff mirror has several interacting branches that could mis-route the WORSE gate.","prompt_body":"Examine every key=value parse loop in `skills/design/scripts/design-plan-quality-assessor.sh`, the Step 3.6 fence in `skills/design/SKILL.md`, and the `apply_step3_6_handoff` function in `skills/design/scripts/test-design-plan-quality-assessor.sh`. Check whether the `%%=*` / `#*=` split correctly handles values that contain `=` (e.g. path-like `ASSESSOR_VERDICT_FILE=/tmp/foo=bar.txt`). Verify the `_assessor_force_stdout` flag is set before the file-read loop so that the file is never read when env write failed. Confirm that WARN lines stored in the result env with embedded `=` signs in the message body are replayed verbatim rather than truncated at the first `=`. Cite specific file paths and line ranges for any issues found, and follow the output-format rules from your outer wrapper exactly.","prompt_body_end":""},{"name":"assess-round-regression","focus_area":"correctness","weight":1,"rationale":"assess-plan-round.sh had read_workflow_path renamed to resolve_workflow_path with new design_classification fallback logic; any callers or test fixtures that relied on the old function name or the old SIMPLE default would silently break.","prompt_body":"Examine the changes to `skills/design/scripts/assess-plan-round.sh`: the rename from `read_workflow_path` to `resolve_workflow_path` and the extraction of the `json_scalar_or_sed` helper. Grep for any remaining references to `read_workflow_path` in the repo. Check whether the new `design_classification` fallback (when `workflow_path` is empty, use `design_classification=HARD` to resolve `HARD`) matches the same fallback in `design-plan-quality-assessor.sh` and in the SKILL.md Step 3.6 fence — all three should agree. Also note that `json_scalar_or_sed` is now duplicated between `assess-plan-round.sh` and `design-plan-quality-assessor.sh`; verify both copies are byte-identical in behavior for the jq → sed fallback chain. Cite specific file paths and line ranges for any issues found, and follow the output-format rules from your outer wrapper exactly.","prompt_body_end":""}]}
